{"ammonia":{"id":"00fbc0d6-f5b3-476a-a004-1229eefebd5a","word":"ammonia","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the compound NH3","tags":["masculine"],"word":"amoníaco"},{"lang":"Brazilian Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the compound NH3","tags":["feminine"],"word":"amônia"},{"lang":"European Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the compound NH3","tags":["feminine"],"word":"amónia"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"topics":["chemistry","inorganic-chemistry","natural-sciences","physical-sciences"],"wikidata":["Q4087"],"senseid":["en:Q4087"],"categories":["en:Inorganic compounds"],"links":[["inorganic chemistry","inorganic chemistry"],["hydrogen","hydrogen"],["nitrogen","nitrogen"]],"raw_glosses":["(inorganic chemistry) A gaseous, toxic compound of hydrogen and nitrogen, NH₃, with a pungent smell and taste."],"glosses":["A gaseous, toxic compound of hydrogen and nitrogen, NH₃, with a pungent smell and taste."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"23e21b45-0ade-4f4d-9d32-daa99159b82d"},{"examples":[{"text":"Never use ammonia to clean metal writing pens.","bold_text_offsets":[[10,17]],"type":"example","id":"e78cb4e7-e97a-4734-b192-539f549a2b2f"},{"text":"Slowly we rode down to the camp - a very sorrowful party. We took \"Nep\" straight to the surgery, where the doctor instantly applied injections of ammonia, then the new remedy for snake bite.","ref":"1887, Harriet W. Daly, Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia, page 95:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[146,153]],"id":"db148661-e117-4424-a0c2-ef6044d0756c"},{"text":"When the woman pressed charges against the man who beat her up and threatened her, the man's girlfriend approached her after work and threw a bottle of ammonia at her.","ref":"1985 December 14, Kim Westheimer, “Rape-Surviving Lesbian Faces Repeated Attacks”, in Gay Community News, volume 13, number 22, page 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[152,159]],"id":"95c8f669-224f-4a1e-8eda-26e5e128d375"}],"links":[["solution","solution"],["water","water"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["A solution of this compound in water used domestically as a cleaning fluid."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"5e6765ae-95f8-4e44-a8c6-7a7d7c9337f2"}],"related":[{"word":"amide"},{"word":"amine"},{"word":"amino-"}],"synonyms":[{"tags":["obsolete"],"word":"spirits of hartshorn"},{"tags":["obsolete"],"word":"volatile alkali"}]},"ammunition":{"id":"8cef28a9-0a4d-4d9d-8ac6-44a4795650a4","word":"ammunition","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"articles used in charging firearms","tags":["feminine"],"word":"munição"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"any stock of missiles","tags":["feminine"],"word":"munição"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Hiro risks turning on a small flashlight, uses it to rummage around the yatcht, picking up valuable stuff: a few bottles of (presumably) drinkable water, some food, extra ammunition for his nine.","ref":"1992, Neal Stephenson, Snow Crash, page 359:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[171,181]],"id":"ae7847a1-75b0-4e9d-b122-7f9c98600420"}],"senseid":["en:Articles used in charging firearms"],"links":[["firearms","firearms"],["ordnance","ordnance"],["powder","powder"],["ball","ball"],["shot","shot"],["shell","shell"],["percussion cap","percussion cap"],["rocket","rocket"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"ammo"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["Articles used in charging firearms and ordnance of all kinds; as powder, balls, shot, shells, percussion caps, rockets, etc."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"5d9649e6-3662-4f10-8960-6336c476cd8a"},{"examples":[{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"ammunition bread","bold_text_offsets":[[0,10]],"type":"example","id":"e30e4da0-3da2-4418-ae49-f2b7b419b65d"},{"tags":["collocation"],"text":"ammunition shoes","bold_text_offsets":[[0,10]],"type":"example","id":"81ab1a37-24ff-47f8-ac71-019353ba591b"}],"categories":["English terms with collocations","English terms with obsolete senses"],"raw_glosses":["(obsolete) Military stores, or provisions of all kinds for attack or defense."],"glosses":["Military stores, or provisions of all kinds for attack or defense."],"tags":["countable","obsolete","uncountable"],"id":"a2a5341c-857b-46d4-a90f-f8e8d4e100d7"},{"examples":[{"text":"They say that the booklet gives them ammunition which is proving effective in breaking down resistance against home building which was created by false propaganda.","ref":"1938, American Lumberman, page 52:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[37,47]],"id":"3b0315b1-c1ac-484d-83e2-d79da7f0688f"},{"text":"As long as the integration fight is in progress, some Southerners are willing to believe anything if it gives them ammunition in their fight to \"retain our traditional way of life.\" If you have any wise bits of philosophy, please pass them along.","ref":"1960, America, Volume 104, America Press, page 697:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[115,125]],"id":"bc584665-ee4e-40ed-8b57-7d514c946052"},{"text":"Providing your administrator(s) with evidence of research progress gives them ammunition to request additional funds from the site-based management pool.","ref":"2005, Blanche Woolls, David V. Loertscher, The Whole School Library Handbook, American Library Association, →ISBN, page 146:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[78,88]],"id":"a0d2df5e-fc8e-4b3b-aade-dcb6ddc5d18d"},{"text":"The first thing to do is NOT constantly defend and argue with the ex or the children. It gives them ammunition and fuels their engines to come after you. In addition, you are just giving them more to use against you.","ref":"2010, Joan Kloth-Zanard, Where Did I Go Wrong? How Did I Miss the Signs? Dealing with Hostile Parenting & Parental Ali